/** \defgroup test_build_run Building and Running Tests
  * \ingroup testing

To build a single test, from inside the `tests` subfolder, run
\verbatim
$ make -B -f Makefile.one t=../apps/zaberCtrl/tests/zaberCtrl_test.cpp
$ ../apps/zaberCtrl/tests/zaberCtrl_test
\endverbatim
which shows how to build the test suite defined in \ref zaberCtrl_test.cpp.  Note that the `.cpp` is not required.  The
`-B` switch for make is not always necessary, but is a good idea to make sure the right things get built.  If you have
only edited the `*_test.cpp` file you can leave `-B` out.

To build all the tests:
\verbatim
$ make
\endverbatim
possibly with the `-B` flag.

Then to run all tests, including the generated logger suites:
\verbatim
$ bash ./testMagAOX.bash
\endverbatim

The runner also works from the repository root:
\verbatim
$ bash tests/testMagAOX.bash
\endverbatim
Alternatively, `make test` from the `tests` directory builds the tests and invokes the same runner.

Each run creates a unique, timestamped directory under `tests/results/`. Previous runs are preserved, and
`tests/results/latest` points to the newest run. These generated results are ignored by git.

- `run.log` saves both stdout and stderr while displaying them in the terminal, including Catch2 assertion failures,
  generated logger build output, and the final failure summary.
- `summary.tsv` records `PASS` or `FAIL`, the exit code, and the executable or logger-suite name for each invocation.
  These are executable-level results; the individual Catch2 case and assertion counts are in `run.log`.

Ordinary test failures, crashes, and missing executables do not skip subsequent tests. The runner returns nonzero if
any invocation fails. The old `tests/test_stderr.txt` is no longer updated; use the saved run directory instead.
Output from test builds performed before invoking the runner is not included in `run.log`.

To inspect the latest run from the repository root:
\verbatim
$ cat tests/results/latest/summary.tsv
$ less tests/results/latest/run.log
\endverbatim

*/

/** \defgroup test_indi Tests of INDI Communications
 * \ingroup testing
 */

